# Images for the Workshop page: one day with the dalmatians, told in four staged photographs and one species card, on the Sanctuary
# of Nelim (the fixture "Nelims-tribe" of Sanctuary Backlot; Nelim is Virginie, the one colonist). Owner rules of 2026-10-06 to
# 2026-11-08 (GALLERY.md, "Shotlist : critères d'une scène à 4/5"): the session is the director, one scenario is one picture, and each
# picture is opened and judged before it reaches the owner. The card (last scenario) is an interface window taken on the bamboo
# backdrop: it is not scored and takes no subtitle; the four photographs are scored a to k in STATUS.md, "Gallery shotlist v3".
#
# THE STORY. WHO: Nelim (Virginie) and her two new dalmatians, Rex the adult and Pup the puppy. WHERE: the Sanctuary, flower garden,
# water garden, salon. WHEN: the day they arrive, 8h, 9h, 15h, 19h, clear weather, the game paused at each shot.
# (1) arrival, she brings them to their new bed; (2) breakfast; (3) Pup out of the pond and a towel; (4) dusk, all three by the fire
# (shotlist v3, STATUS.md, 2026-11-08). Nelim keeps the teal shirt, brown trousers all day (continuity) and her own NSB hairstyle (no change: a colonist property). Clothes and
# expressions are suggestions (owner, 2026-10-25): default expression smiling. No apparel on the animals (collar probe ebfe failed,
# 2026-10-25): the dalmatians stay vanilla. The dog bed is More animal beds (Animal.BedsNew, 3107972819), in the DepMap of this pass.
#
# THE SHOTLIST (one line per photograph, checked against the scenarios by scripts/Check-ShotlistVsScenario.ps1):
#
#   1. arrival: flower-garden path at 8h, clear, +60 ticks. The dirt path along the south edge, the bed GSAnimalBedBig (154, 99) south of it.
#         Decor: the bed alone (no hay on it: the hay lies beside it); the fixture IncenseShrine within 1 cells of (158, 102), SculptureGrand and SculptureLarge within 2 cells of (153, 100) are hidden; the lamps, daylilies and tall grass are the ones the z3 fixture
#         already holds (nothing else placed: a cell with a plant or a lamp fails the placement), flower beds behind.
#         Nelim Apparel_CollarShirt rgb (22, 110, 115), Apparel_Pants rgb (74, 58, 50), MouthSmile, LidCheerful.
#         Action (v5): Nelim STANDS at (156, 101) facing South (set again after the ticks: she drifted north in 1ddd) toward the camera, smiling, face clear (a carried item hid it in 6d59 and fe07, so no haul here);
#         3 Hay lie on the path at (152, 101) beside the bed, delivered. Rex walks to (155, 101) then stands facing South toward the camera; Pup walks from (154, 104) to (153, 100), lower half of the frame
#         beside Rex. The instant: the bed waits empty, the hay is delivered beside it. Zoom 3.2 on (155, 100), the bed in frame, Pup stands at (154, 100) facing South beside Rex: Rex about 15 percent of the height, readable at 268 px.
#         Says: Nelim brings the dalmatians to their new bed. THUMBNAIL: Rex about 12 percent of the height.
#   2. breakfast: the same path at 9h, clear. The same z3 lamps and plants, bed (154, 99) in the foreground (lower z), a Kibble stack. Nelim in the same outfit Apparel_CollarShirt rgb (22, 110, 115), Apparel_Pants
#         rgb (74, 58, 50), smile. Action (v5, as scenario 1): Nelim STANDS at (155, 102) facing South, smiling, and both dogs are set again after the ticks (they walked past in a401); 5 Kibble lie at (154, 100); Rex
#         walks from (154, 104) to (154, 101) toward the camera, facing it; Pup stands at (153, 100) facing East, nose to the kibble. The fixture IncenseShrine within 1 cells of (158, 102), SculptureGrand and SculptureLarge within 2 cells of (153, 100) are hidden.
#         Zoom 2.2 on (154, 100). Says: breakfast for the dalmatians. THUMBNAIL: Rex about 20 percent of the height.
#   3. towel: water-garden west bank at 15h, clear. Willows, reeds, lily pads, the pond's ducks (not removed), Plant_Daylily at (146, 171)
#         and (147, 169), Plant_YellowTallGrass at (146, 173), (148, 170) and (150, 168) so the bank is not bare, a Cloth lies at (151, 171) beside her, the fixture SteamGeyser within 1 cells of (149, 173) is hidden.
#         Nelim same outfit Apparel_CollarShirt rgb (22, 110, 115), Apparel_Pants rgb (74, 58, 50), smile.
#         Action (v5, as scenarios 1 and 2): Nelim STANDS at (151, 172) facing South, smiling, no haul, set again after 60 ticks; Pup walks out of the shallows from (154, 170) to (152, 170)
#         and is set again at (152, 171) facing West. The instant: Pup has just stepped out of the pond, the towel lies ready. Zoom 2.8 on (151, 171).
#         Says: Pup out of the water, Nelim brings the towel. THUMBNAIL: Pup about 20 percent of the height.
#   4. fire: sofa corner of the salon at 19h, clear (v11, cells read in the 1cb4 free-cells listing; 4c put the bed indoors behind a wall, the story broke).#         The fixture Campfire at (194, 121) lit (no torch: the cells are taken), the bed GSAnimalBedBig near (193, 119) on the same stone floor.#         Nelim same outfit Apparel_CollarShirt rgb (22, 110, 115), Apparel_Pants rgb (74, 58, 50), a small calm smile MouthLipsSmallSmile, LidNormal.#         Action: Nelim STANDS at (193, 121) facing South, no haul, set again after 60 ticks; a WoodLog lies at (194, 122) by the fire; Rex stands at (194, 120)#         facing South toward the camera (set again after the ticks), Pup stands at (193, 120) facing South, the bed (193, 119) behind them (4g: Pup asleep sat half out of the frame). Zoom 1.8 on (193, 120), warm low light.#         Says: all three at the fire, the bed is theirs now. THUMBNAIL: Rex about 25 percent, Pup about 15 percent of the height.
#         The fixture Campfire at (194, 121) lit (no torch: the cells are taken), the bed GSAnimalBedBig near (193, 119) on the same stone floor.
#         Nelim same outfit Apparel_CollarShirt rgb (22, 110, 115), Apparel_Pants rgb (74, 58, 50), a small calm smile MouthLipsSmallSmile, LidNormal.
#         Action: Nelim STANDS at (193, 121) facing South, no haul, set again after 60 ticks; a WoodLog lies at (194, 122) by the fire; Rex stands at (194, 120)
#         facing South toward the camera (set again after the ticks), Pup stands at (193, 120) facing South, the bed (193, 119) behind them (4g: Pup asleep sat half out of the frame). Zoom 1.8 on (193, 120), warm low light.
#         Says: all three at the fire, the bed is theirs now. THUMBNAIL: Rex about 25 percent, Pup about 15 percent of the height.
#
# GESTURE RECIPE (NPT ticket 531b, proven 2026-10-25, fix 6c8ba9d): force the walk or the haul, then
# `I advance the paused game by exactly N ticks` (20 ticks is about one cell), then frame and shoot. The pawns are caught in stride.
# North is a HIGHER z: a walk toward the camera ends on a LOWER z (capture db7c walked away by mistake). Nelim's face steps come
# last, after the ticks (the face of db7c frowned with them first). The ticks and the cells are first guesses: judge each capture and
# adjust. A cell that is not standable fails the spawn step by name.
#
#   - Staged only by wsl-deps.sanctuary.map. Every other pass skips this feature. Run it in English.
#   - Photographs show the map alone (the game's own screenshot mode): the mod adds an animal, not an interface.
#   - What a capture shows that comes from the scene or the shared tools (a pile counter, a name left on screen, a zone painted on
#     the floor) is not worked around here: it goes to NPT with the capture, and the picture is not kept.
#   - The runner starts the game with developer mode on: it is turned off before each capture.
@requires:nelim.pickletools.stagedecor @requires:nelim.pickletools.camerazoom @requires:nelim.pickletools.screenshotstudio @requires:nelim.pickletools.screenshotmode @requires:nelim.pickletools.clickdiagnostics @requires:nelim.pickletools.colonistrace @review
